    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 the single test class `AcceptanceTest` (the only test in the suite) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter so the code persists and is returned on `GET`.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four platform schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in `schema.sql`.\n\n3. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `readOnly` `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically on the response.\n\n4. **New pipeline step** (`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 computes `LAST3` as the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `NNNN` as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current owner count), formatted `%s-%04d`. It runs **before** `SaveOwner`, so the new owner is excluded from the count.\n\n5. **POST pipeline YAML** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step (under `transaction` governance) between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`.\n\n6. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"customerCode\", ignore = true)` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` since it's a server-assigned field, not a request input (also clears the unmapped-target warning).\n\nThe sequence is global and monotonic: the first owner (`smithers`) gets `SMI-000N`, and the next (`jones`) gets `JON-000(N+1)`, satisfying the test's increment-by-one assertion.",
